Ashford Castle in Cong, County Mayo has been named the World's Most Beautiful Hotel and Best Heritage Hotel by Time Out for 2026.  

This 800 year old fortress on the shores of Lough Corrib began life in 1228 under the Anglo Norman de Burgo family. It later became the cherished country seat of the Guinness family, who expanded the estate, planted thousands of trees and shaped the grand Victorian Gothic character that still defines it today. Guests over the centuries have included Oscar Wilde, King George V, Ronald Reagan and countless others drawn to its fairytale setting.  

In 2013 the Tollman family, founders of Red Carnation Hotels, acquired the property and invested heavily in a sensitive restoration that revived every corridor, chandelier and garden while preserving its soul. Under the steady leadership of Managing Director Niall Rochford and the dedicated team, the 350 acre estate now offers 83 uniquely designed rooms and suites, a spa pool ringed with seashells, private cinema, secret gardens and activities from falconry to lake cruises, all delivered with genuine Irish warmth.  

Set between Mayo and Galway on the Wild Atlantic Way, this is more than a hotel. It is living history, impeccable hospitality and pure enchantment rolled into one unmissable experience.  

